      "content": "Stop and listen carefully: waiting for another episode or trying to distinguish between a migraine and a stroke is extremely dangerous because a full-blown stroke can happen at any moment without warning. The symptoms you were describing (sudden vision loss and one-sided clumsiness) are specific red flags that require immediate evaluation, not just self-monitoring. Even if you are 100% normal now, going to the ER or calling 911/999 ensures you get the correct treatment quickly and prevents permanent brain damage. Please prioritize your brain health over saving money or time today.",
